  <subsection title="Add and subtract rational functions">
    <p>To add or subtract rational functions, we use the same techniques we used to add or subtract polynomial functions.</p>
    <example number="7.23">
      <problem>
        <p>Find $$R(x) = f(x) - g(x)$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{x + 5}{x - 2}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{5x + 18}{x^{2} - 4}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Substitute in the functions $$f(x),$$$$g(x).$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the denominators.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Do the expressions have a common denominator? No.Rewrite each expression with the LCD.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>$$\begin{array}{lccl} \text{Find the LCD.} &amp; &amp; &amp; \begin{array}{l} {x - 2\mspace{9mu} = (x - 2)} \\ \underset{\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_}{x^{2}-4=(x-2)(x+2)} \\ {\mspace{13mu}\text{LCD} = (x - 2)(x + 2)} \end{array} \end{array}$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite each rational expression as anequivalent rational expression with the LCD.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Write as one rational expression.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Factor the numerator, and removecommon factors.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="7.45">
      <p>Find $$R(x) = f(x) - g(x)$$ where $$f(x) = \frac{x + 1}{x + 3}$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{x + 17}{x^{2} - x - 12}.$$</p>
